From 1c26ee1e45a3b795649bafe78132a5a3cb2e4895 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:41:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] NO-AIR: hands on real things in the opening film and in
 the residents' work

The opening: the lift gets a control with a lever the worker's hand throws; the crate comes down with both
his hands on it; Twinsen's screwdriver turns a screw on the lamp's collar; Arthur's boat stands on a building
crate and he seats the mast with his own hand; Zoe's palms press the tray's soil; the screwdriver is laid
where it lies. The film's length, shot times, lines and flags are unchanged. tests/opening.mjs item 11
measures each contact against the drawn triangles (tests/lib/contact.js).

The game: a layer on every NPC's rig puts working hands on the table, crate, rim or wall in front of them
(src/game/workhands.js on src/engine/handik.js), work stops are stood at an arm's length from their thing,
a track's walk ends on its spot, and an action with nothing in reach is stood down instead of mimed.
tests/no-air.mjs sweeps every person's hand actions over the chapters. Work in progress: see
docs/lba-maturity/no-air.md for what is measured and what is left.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
